@page "/about"
<PageTitle>About · StudyFlow</PageTitle>
<div class="page-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">PROJECT INFORMATION</div><h1>About StudyFlow</h1><p>A student-centered assignment organizer built with Blazor and C#.</p></div></div>
<section class="surface about-panel"><div class="about-logo">✳</div><h2>Study smarter. Stay organized.</h2>
<p>StudyFlow is a practical educational project that helps students manage assignments, organize courses, plan deadlines, and record focused study time. It is designed for an individual student and stores data locally in a JSON file.</p>
<div class="about-points">
    <div><strong>Blazor Interactive Server</strong><span>Responsive, interactive user interface</span></div>
    <div><strong>C# / .NET 10</strong><span>Business rules, validation and application services</span></div>
    <div><strong>Local persistence</strong><span>JSON file with atomic replacement on save</span></div>
    <div><strong>Explainable focus suggestions</strong><span>Priority + deadlines + current progress</span></div>
</div>
<h3>Privacy and scope</h3><p>StudyFlow does not require a login, internet service, or paid subscription. It is intended for local single-user use. Do not deploy it publicly without adding authentication and suitable multi-user storage.</p>
